# Pinned SSH host keys for the MemHamWAN RouterOS fleet (port 222).
#
# Source of truth for fleet host-key trust: merge into your own
# ~/.ssh/known_hosts with
#   cd ansible && ansible-playbook playbooks/seed_known_hosts.yml
# Ansible's network_cli transport (libssh) negotiates the ssh-rsa host key
# and cannot prompt on first contact — without a pinned rsa entry it fails.
# The ROS 7.12 fleet offers ssh-rsa host keys only.
#
# Seeded 2026-08-29 by scanning from rpi.sco (the host whose nightly backups
# already verify these devices); every key that root@rpi.sco had previously
# stored matched exactly, zero mismatches. Dark sites are absent — re-scan
# from rpi.sco and append as they recover:
#   ssh-keyscan -p 222 -t rsa <host>
# A changed line in this file means a device host key changed: that is a PR
# diff worth interrogating before accepting.
